1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-6","kind":"phase-index","route":"/roadmap/phase-6","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-6","sourceHash":"292e08557bceb885081954e493c14c72793140e4ae749992c70740aed6f2ac9b","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:12:01.341Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Fluency","zh":"流利度"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can speak, write, read, and listen. You can have real conversations, express complex ideas, and catch most of your own mistakes. But using the language still takes <em>effort</em> and have more practice to do. Phase 6 is about removing that effort with lots of practice.","zh":"你已经能够说、写、读、听，也能进行真实对话、表达复杂想法，并发现自己大多数的错误。但使用这门语言仍然需要<em>努力</em>，还有很多练习要做。第 6 阶段的重点，就是通过大量练习消除这种努力感。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The goal of the Refold roadmap is to lead you to \"functional fluency\" — the ability to live your life entirely in the target language without it significantly impacting your ability to function. The language stops being a project and starts being a part of who you are. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/functional-fluency\">Functional Fluency</a>","zh":"Refold 路线图的目标，是带你达到“功能性流利”——也就是完全用目标语言生活，同时不会明显影响你的正常生活能力。语言不再是一项任务，而会成为你身份的一部分。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/functional-fluency\">功能性流利</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"However, that doesn't mean it needs to be YOUR goal. Many learners are thrilled to just <em>reach</em> Phase 6 and are satisfied with that level of fluency. It's totally up to you to continue with your focused study of the language, change things up or start with a new language! But we recommend you read Phase 6 anyway so that you can implement some of the suggestions into your daily routine so your ability continues to increase, even if it's a bit more slowly.","zh":"不过，这并不意味着它必须成为你的目标。许多学习者只要<em>达到</em>第 6 阶段，就已经非常满意于这样的流利程度。你完全可以自行决定，是继续专注学习这门语言、换一种学习方式，还是开始学习一门新语言！但我们仍然建议你阅读第 6 阶段的内容，这样你可以把其中一些建议融入日常安排，让自己的能力继续提升，即使速度慢一些。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This phase is less about learning new things and more about doing a <em>lot</em> of what you already know how to do. Volume and variety are the keys. Your level will be roughly equivalent to C1 by the end. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR Levels</a>","zh":"这个阶段与其说是学习新东西，不如说是大量<em>练习</em>你已经会做的事情。数量和多样性是关键。到阶段结束时，你的水平大致相当于 C1。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR 等级</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"","zh":"","header":true},{"en":"Cousin","zh":"近亲","header":true},{"en":"Similar","zh":"相近","header":true},{"en":"Neutral","zh":"中性","header":true},{"en":"Distant","zh":"遥远","header":true}],[{"en":"This phase","zh":"本阶段","header":false},{"en":"135","zh":"135","header":false},{"en":"225","zh":"225","header":false},{"en":"300","zh":"300","header":false},{"en":"450","zh":"450","header":false}],[{"en":"Cumulative","zh":"累计","header":false},{"en":"800","zh":"800","header":false},{"en":"1350","zh":"1350","header":false},{"en":"1700","zh":"1700","header":false},{"en":"2700","zh":"2700","header":false}]]},{"id":"sub-phases","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Sub-phases","zh":"子阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>6A — Output Automaticity:</strong> Make your speech and writing effortless through massive amounts of practice.","zh":"<strong>6A——输出自动化：</strong>通过大量练习，让说和写变得毫不费力。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>6B — Vocabulary Gaps:</strong> Fill in the everyday vocabulary you're still missing — the words you can never remember when you need them.","zh":"<strong>6B——词汇缺口：</strong>补齐你仍然缺少的日常词汇——那些在需要时总是想不起来的词。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>6C — Lots of Practice:</strong> Reinforce everything through high-volume practice of both input and output.","zh":"<strong>6C——大量练习：</strong>通过高强度练习输入和输出，巩固所有能力。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Phase 6 is built on Skill Acquisition Theory, particularly <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780203628942\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DeKeyser's (2007, 2015)</a> research on how language skills develop from controlled (conscious) to automatic (unconscious) processing. At your current level, you have the knowledge and accuracy needed to communicate effectively. The massive practice in this phase is what transforms that knowledge into the automatic fluency that characterizes near-native speakers.","zh":"第 6 阶段建立在技能习得理论之上，尤其参考了<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780203628942\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DeKeyser（2007、2015）</a>关于语言技能如何从受控（有意识）加工发展为自动化（无意识）加工的研究。在你目前的水平上，你已经具备有效沟通所需的知识和准确性。本阶段的大量练习，会把这些知识转化为接近母语者特征的自动化流利能力。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The emphasis on vocabulary expansion reflects <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/cmlr.63.1.59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation's (2006)</a> research on lexical coverage thresholds. Nation found that roughly 8,000–9,000 word families are needed for unassisted reading comprehension, and 6,000–7,000 for listening. While lower vocabulary counts are sufficient for basic conversation, reaching functional fluency requires the expanded vocabulary that typically comes only after thousands of hours of engaged input and output.","zh":"对词汇扩展的重视，反映了<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/cmlr.63.1.59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation（2006）</a>关于词汇覆盖率阈值的研究。Nation 发现，要在没有辅助的情况下理解书面内容，大约需要 8000—9000 个词族；听力理解则需要 6000—7000 个词族。虽然基础对话所需的词汇量更少，但要达到功能性流利，仍需要不断扩大的词汇量，而这通常只有经过数千小时投入式输入和输出才能获得。"}}],"cards":[{"href":"/roadmap/phase-6/6a-output-automaticity","title":{"en":"6AOutput Automaticity","zh":"6A输出自动化"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-6/6b-vocabulary-gaps","title":{"en":"6BVocabulary Gaps","zh":"6B词汇空缺"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-6/6c-lots-of-practice","title":{"en":"6CLots of Practice","zh":"6C大量练习"}}]}}]
